IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Transferred Officers' Allowances Act 1948 (Cth), as amended to 1956.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1948A00020.txt. Seat: the transferred
-- officer or widow. Amounts in pounds a year.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Transferred officer case` HAS
    `annual pension`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `on`                                                IS A DATE
    `a widow`                                           IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 4
@ref s 4
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 4 allowance on` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p AT MOST 288  THEN p DIVIDED BY 4
        IF p LESS THAN 360 THEN 360 MINUS p
        OTHERWISE               0

-- s 5
@ref s 5
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5 allowance on` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p GREATER THAN 702 THEN 0
        IF s AT MOST 260      THEN s DIVIDED BY 5
        IF s AT MOST 650      THEN 52
        IF p LESS THAN 702    THEN 702 MINUS p
        OTHERWISE                  0
    WHERE
        s MEANS p PLUS `the s 4 allowance on` p

-- s 6 (12 November 1955 to 31 December 1956)
@ref s 6
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 6 allowance on` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF t AT MOST 156 THEN 52
        IF t AT MOST 312 THEN t DIVIDED BY 6 PLUS 26
        IF t AT MOST 448 THEN 78
        IF t AT MOST 500 THEN IF 526 MINUS t GREATER THAN 52 THEN 526 MINUS t ELSE 52
        OTHERWISE             52
    WHERE
        t MEANS p PLUS `the s 4 allowance on` p PLUS `the s 5 allowance on` p

@ref ss 4-7
@export default The allowances payable to me as a transferred officer (or widow) under the Transferred Officers' Allowances Act 1948 (Cth), as amended, at a given date: the s 4 and s 5 allowances on my pension or retiring allowance, and, between 12 November 1955 and 31 December 1956, the s 6 allowance; half of each for a widow (s 7). NOTHING before 31 October 1953, whose rates are not in the text. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Transferred officer case`  @desc The annual pension (the husband's for a widow), the date, and whether a widow
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my allowances for` c MEANS
    IF c's `on` LESS THAN Date 31 10 1953
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (share TIMES (base PLUS s6))
    WHERE
        p MEANS c's `annual pension`
        base MEANS `the s 4 allowance on` p PLUS `the s 5 allowance on` p
        s6 MEANS IF c's `on` AT LEAST Date 12 11 1955 AND c's `on` AT MOST Date 31 12 1956 THEN `the s 6 allowance on` p ELSE 0
        share MEANS IF c's `a widow` THEN 1/2 ELSE 1
